### [Unreleased]

* fix: consul `--auth-token` is sent as the ACL token (and wins over `CONSUL_HTTP_TOKEN` / `CONSUL_HTTP_TOKEN_FILE`), etcd `--auth-token` is passed to the etcd client as a JWT (an error together with `--basic-auth`), and redis `--username` authenticates as that ACL user with the password; all three used to be accepted and dropped, as were `auth_token` and `username` in confd.toml. Redis `--basic-auth`, `--auth-token`, `--client-cert` and `--client-ca-keys` stay unused (confd has no redis TLS support) and, like `basic_auth`, `auth_token`, `client_cert` and `client_cakeys` set for any backend that does not use them, now log `--<flag> has no effect with the <backend> backend` at startup. **Migration:** an `auth_token` in confd.toml is now sent by consul and etcd, and a `username` by redis; remove it if it was not meant for that backend (#689)
* chore: anchor the `confd` binary pattern in `.gitignore` to the repository root (`/confd`); the bare pattern also matched the `cmd/confd/` directory, so new files there were left out of `git status` and had to be force-added
* test: every backend command builds its `backends.Config` in one `backendConfig` method that both `Run` and the tests call, replacing the tests' own copies of each mapping; a new test sets every mapped flag of every command and compares the whole config, so dropping any field from a command fails it (#685)
* fix: read `batch_interval` and `imds_cache_ttl` from confd.toml; both were documented but ignored. `--batch-interval` / `CONFD_BATCH_INTERVAL` and `--imds-cache-ttl` still win over the file, and an invalid duration in either key is a startup error (#680)
* refactor: remove `processEnv()`; `CONFD_CLIENT_CERT`, `CONFD_CLIENT_KEY` and `CONFD_CLIENT_CAKEYS` reach consul, etcd, vault and redis only through their flags, with the same precedence as every other setting. An empty `--client-cert=`, `--client-key=` or `--client-ca-keys=` is now an explicit value and wins over the environment variable; it used to fall back to the variable (#682)
* docs: say that `{{.src}}` in `check_cmd` is the staged file and that `{{.dest}}` is not available there (#676)
* fix: for string settings, an environment variable set to an empty value is treated as unset, so the value from confd.toml or the built-in default applies; previously it suppressed the file's value, `CONFD_CONFDIR=` made confd look for `conf.d` in the current directory, and `CONFD_FAILURE_MODE=` was a startup error (#675)
* chore: lint the packages behind the `e2e` build tag (`run.build-tags` in `.golangci.yml`, so `make lint` and the lint workflow both cover them) and fix the 15 wrapcheck and errorlint findings in `test/e2e` (#674)
* fix: `{{.src}}` in `reload_cmd` names a file that exists: the destination path, or the kept stage file with `--keep-stage-file`; it used to be the stage path after the file had been moved (#667)
* docs: only the `test/e2e/watch` package needs Docker; show how to run the other e2e packages without it (#658)
* chore: set an explicit wrapcheck `ignore-sigs` list in `.golangci.yml` (`.Errorf(`, `errors.New(`, `errors.Unwrap(`, `errors.Join(`, `.Wrap(`, `.Wrapf(`) in place of the linter's built-in defaults; no findings change (#657)
* docs: document that confd.toml accepts `log-level` / `log-format` alongside `log_level` / `log_format`, that the underscore spelling takes precedence when it is non-empty, and that an empty underscore value falls back to the hyphenated one; add tests for both and for flag and env overrides (#656)
* fix: Secrets Manager errors served from the per-call error cache keep the `get secret value "<name>":` prefix added on the first failure (#655)
* fix: `ACM_EXPORT_PRIVATE_KEY` is parsed as a boolean; any non-empty value, including `false` and `0`, used to enable private key export and override an explicit `--acm-export-private-key=false` (#660)
* fix: the redis backend authenticates with `--password`, `REDIS_PASSWORD` or `password` in confd.toml; previously only `--client-key` / `client_key` / `CONFD_CLIENT_KEY` carried the password. Precedence is `--password`, `REDIS_PASSWORD`, confd.toml `password`, then the legacy client key, and an empty value is treated as unset. **Migration:** a `password` key in confd.toml that redis used to ignore is now sent and wins over `client_key`; remove it if it is not the redis password (#661)
* fix: log a startup warning (`--<flag> has no effect with the <backend> backend`) when `--dial-timeout`, `--read-timeout`, `--write-timeout`, `--retry-max-attempts`, `--retry-base-delay` or `--retry-max-delay` is supplied for a backend that does not use it; `--help` and the docs now state each flag's scope (the read/write timeout and retry flags apply to redis only) (#662)
* docs: describe debounce as what the code does, a fixed delay after a change (about once per debounce period under continuous changes), not a timer that resets; batch mode does not apply per-resource debounce. A test pins the behavior (#663)
* fix: a failed `reload_cmd` is retried the next time the resource is processed, even though the destination is already in sync; the state is in memory and the retry stops after the first success. Under `--failure-mode fail-fast` in interval mode, a reload that keeps failing stops the resources after it on every cycle (#664)
* fix: interval, watch and batch-watch modes exit non-zero when they stop because no template resource could be loaded, including after a SIGHUP reload. With `--onetime`, load errors follow `--failure-mode`: best-effort processes the resources that loaded and exits non-zero, fail-fast processes none. Load errors now name every file that failed, which also changes the `--preflight` error text (#665)
* fix: a failing `check_cmd` reports `config check failed:` once instead of twice; remove two debug log calls in config loading that could never print; correct the sample output in `docs/noop-mode.md` (#666)
* fix: watch mode with a polling-only backend (acm, dynamodb, env, imds, secretsmanager, ssm, vault) now fails at startup with `watch mode not supported for <backend> backend`, for the global backend and for per-resource `[backend]` sections, whether watch is set by `--watch`, `CONFD_WATCH` or `watch = true` in confd.toml, and also with `--onetime` and `--preflight`; previously vault and env blocked silently and `watch = true` in confd.toml bypassed the per-command checks (#604)
* refactor: watch support is an optional `backends.Watcher` interface; `StoreClient` no longer includes `WatchPrefix` and `types.NoopWatcher` is removed (#604)
* fix: stop, reload and context cancellation no longer wait out `--watch-error-backoff` while a watch backend is erroring; watch and batch-watch modes share one monitor/reload implementation (#605)
* fix: `check_cmd` and `reload_cmd` strings are logged only at debug level; info, warn and error records identify the command by type and destination. Remove the legacy `runCommand` helper so there is one command execution path (#607)
* refactor: `backends.New` takes a `context.Context` and the acm, dynamodb, ssm, secretsmanager and imds constructors use it in place of `context.Background()` (#608)
* fix: SIGINT or SIGTERM while the global backend client is being constructed cancels startup and exits 1 with `startup interrupted: received signal <signal>` instead of leaving a hung constructor running; per-resource `[backend]` clients are built later and are not covered (#608)
* test: cover Kong source tracking, config precedence and `applyBackendDefaults()` through production code paths; remove default-node tests that never called production code (#610)
* docs: add a troubleshooting guide (`docs/troubleshooting.md`); document that `check_cmd`/`reload_cmd` run through a shell (#344, #607)
* fix: read `backend_timeout`, `check_cmd_timeout`, `reload_cmd_timeout`, `shutdown_timeout`, `debounce`, `systemd_notify` and `watchdog_interval` from confd.toml, and accept `log_level`/`log_format` alongside `log-level`/`log-format`; these keys were documented but ignored
* fix: wrap returned errors with context and compare errors with `errors.Is`/`errors.As` across `pkg/` and `cmd/confd` (clears all wrapcheck and errorlint findings); error messages gain context prefixes such as `create store client: initialize etcd backend: ...`
* fix: `make integration` now runs the file backend scripts (`test_yaml.sh`, `test_json.sh`)
* fix(test): integration templates resolve the loopback interface name per host (`CONFD_TEST_LOOPBACK_IFACE`, default `lo`) so the standalone integration checks pass on macOS
* ci: add golangci-lint workflow and drop the invalid `linters-settings` block from `.golangci.yml`
* chore(deps): move from go.yaml.in/yaml/v3 to go.yaml.in/yaml/v4 v4.0.0
* docs: remove the unsupported `backend` key and hyphenated keys from confd.toml examples; correct watch-mode support (env is polling only), the integration/e2e test layout, and `--watch` examples for the env and Vault backends

